description:
Objective: run every one of the 20 frozen CQ-M03 workloads once (n=1) through the CQ-M04b driver (task-9cfaacf11e194062bc1ca5f77388ec90), then publish the baseline outcome report built by CQ-M04 (task-0ece1a3552944298af911356f149e150). Use the human-approved configuration from comment-700a6a5111ad4a57a3340a2dac0ab586 on task-0ece1a3552944298af911356f149e150:
- today's model/effort defaults;
- one run per workload;
- a 60-minute wall-clock cap per workload;
- capped runs are recorded with their partial counters;
- missing counters stay unknown.
This is the execution slice split from CQ-M04 by size.

Deliverable:
- 20 outcome records, 5 per category, that pass the CQ-M04 validator;
- their usage receipts, archived (allowlisted fields only; no prompts, tool arguments, secrets or prices);
- the generated report as JSON plus markdown, committed under one documented results path, e.g. docs/baselines/cq-m04-<date>/.
The report must regenerate byte-identically from the archived inputs with the CQ-M04 CLI.

Operational note: this needs a signed-in claude CLI and real paid usage, and can take up to about 20 hours of wall-clock time (20 x 60-minute cap). When promoting this BACKLOG row, a human decides when and where it runs (operator-run, or agent-run in the background with checkpoints).

NOT in scope:
- changing workloads, rubrics, the driver or report code;
- reruns beyond n=1 (an infrastructure failure is recorded, never silently retried);
- new-profile or verified-local runs;
- any savings, quality-improvement or statistical-significance claim.

Verification: node scripts/analyze-baseline.mjs --records <archived records dir> --project <archived usage dir> --expected <frozen manifest> --json must reproduce the committed report JSON byte-for-byte (exit 0), and node --test scripts/tests/usage-report.test.mjs must exit 0.
